```

### Rules for Message Files
- One JSON file per locale: `messages/{locale}.json`
- Organize keys by feature namespace (PascalCase): `Dashboard`, `Billing`, `Pricing`
- Keep key paths shallow (max 3 levels deep)
- Use ICU message syntax for pluralization and formatting
- All locales MUST have identical key structures — missing keys break at runtime
- Never put HTML in translation strings; use rich text formatting instead

## Pluralization & Formatting

### ICU Message Syntax
```json
{
  "Pricing": {
    "features": {
      "projects": "{count, plural, one {# project} other {# projects}}",
      "storage": "{amount, number} MB storage",
      "trialDays": "{days, plural, =0 {Trial expired} one {# day left} other {# days left}}"
    }
  },
  "Billing": {
    "nextPayment": "Next payment: {date, date, medium}",
    "amount": "{amount, number, ::currency/USD}"
  }
}
```

### Usage in Components
```typescript
const t = useTranslations('Pricing.features');
t('projects', { count: 5 });      // "5 projects"
t('projects', { count: 1 });      // "1 project"
t('trialDays', { days: 0 });      // "Trial expired"
```

### Rich Text (instead of HTML in strings)
```typescript
// In JSON: "terms": "By signing up you agree to our <link>Terms of Service</link>"
t.rich('terms', {
  link: (chunks) => <a href="/terms">{chunks}</a>,
});
```

## Dynamic Locale Switching

Use the locale-aware `Link` and `useRouter` from `i18n/navigation.ts`:

```typescript
'use client';

import { useLocale } from 'next-intl';
import { usePathname, useRouter } from '@/i18n/navigation';
import { routing } from '@/i18n/routing';

export function LocaleSwitcher() {
  const locale = useLocale();
  const pathname = usePathname();
  const router = useRouter();

  function handleChange(newLocale: string) {
    router.replace(pathname, { locale: newLocale });
  }

  return (
    <select value={locale} onChange={(e) => handleChange(e.target.value)}>
      {routing.locales.map((loc) => (
        <option key={loc} value={loc}>
          {loc.toUpperCase()}
        </option>
      ))}
    </select>
  );
}
```

## SEO: Metadata, hreflang, and Sitemaps

### Translated Metadata per Page
```typescript
// app/[locale]/pricing/page.tsx
import { getTranslations, setRequestLocale } from 'next-intl/server';
import { routing } from '@/i18n/routing';
import type { Metadata } from 'next';

type Props = { params: Promise<{ locale: string }> };

export async function generateMetadata({ params }: Props): Promise<Metadata> {
  const { locale } = await params;
  const t = await getTranslations({ locale, namespace: 'Metadata' });
  const host = 'https://cvfairy.com';

  const languages: Record<string, string> = {};
  for (const loc of routing.locales) {
    languages[loc] = `${host}/${loc}/pricing`;
  }
  languages['x-default'] = `${host}/${routing.defaultLocale}/pricing`;

  return {
    title: t('title'),
    description: t('description'),
    alternates: {
      canonical: `${host}/${locale}/pricing`,
      languages,
    },
  };
}
```

### hreflang Rules
- Always include `x-default` pointing to your default locale — Google requires this for clarity
- Use `localePrefix: 'always'` so every locale has an explicit URL path (no ambiguity)
- All redirects should use 308 (permanent) to preserve HTTP method
- Generate hreflang in `generateMetadata` using `alternates.languages`

### Sitemap with Locale Alternates
```typescript
// app/sitemap.ts
import { MetadataRoute } from 'next';
import { routing } from '@/i18n/routing';
import { getPathname } from '@/i18n/navigation';

const host = 'https://cvfairy.com';

const pages = ['/', '/pricing', '/about', '/contact'];

export default async function sitemap(): Promise<MetadataRoute.Sitemap> {
  return pages.flatMap((page) =>
    routing.locales.map((locale) => {
      const languages: Record<string, string> = {};
      for (const loc of routing.locales) {
        languages[loc] = `${host}/${loc}${page === '/' ? '' : page}`;
      }
      languages['x-default'] = `${host}/${routing.defaultLocale}${page === '/' ? '' : page}`;

      return {
        url: `${host}/${locale}${page === '/' ? '' : page}`,
        lastModified: new Date(),
        alternates: { languages },
      };
    })
  );
}
```

## Static Rendering

- Call `setRequestLocale(locale)` at the top of every page and layout under `[locale]`
- Export `generateStaticParams` from the root locale layout to pre-render all locales
- Without `setRequestLocale`, next-intl falls back to dynamic rendering via headers
- This is a temporary workaround until next-intl removes the limitation

```typescript
// Required in every page.tsx and layout.tsx under [locale]
export default async function Page({ params }: Props) {
  const { locale } = await params;
  setRequestLocale(locale); // MUST be first — enables static rendering
  // ...
}
```

## Next.js 16+ with next/root-params

If using Next.js 16.3+, you can use `next/root-params` to simplify the request config:

```typescript
// i18n/request.ts (Next.js 16.3+)
import * as rootParams from 'next/root-params';
import { getRequestConfig } from 'next-intl/server';
import { hasLocale } from 'next-intl';
import { routing } from './routing';
import { notFound } from 'next/navigation';

export default getRequestConfig(async () => {
  const paramValue = await rootParams.locale();
  const locale = hasLocale(routing.locales, paramValue) ? paramValue : routing.defaultLocale;

  if (!hasLocale(routing.locales, paramValue)) notFound();

  return {
    locale,
    messages: (await import(`../messages/${locale}.json`)).default,
  };
});
```

This eliminates the need for `setRequestLocale` in every page/layout.

## Route Handlers & Server Actions

```typescript
// app/api/newsletter/route.ts
import { getTranslations } from 'next-intl/server';

export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const { locale } = await request.json();
  const t = await getTranslations({ locale, namespace: 'Newsletter' });

  return Response.json({ message: t('subscribed') });
}
```

## Anti-Patterns — NEVER Do These

- Do NOT use `next-i18next` with App Router — it only works with Pages Router
- Do NOT skip `setRequestLocale` in pages/layouts (causes dynamic rendering fallback)
- Do NOT put HTML in translation strings — use `t.rich()` with render functions
- Do NOT hardcode locale strings in components — always use `t()` or the routing config
- Do NOT create locale-specific component files (`PricingEn.tsx`, `PricingEs.tsx`)
- Do NOT use `localePrefix: 'as-needed'` unless you have a specific SEO reason — it creates URL ambiguity
- Do NOT forget `x-default` in hreflang alternates
- Do NOT nest translation keys more than 3 levels deep
- Do NOT lazy-load message files per namespace in App Router — load all messages in the layout
- Do NOT mix `useTranslations` (client) and `getTranslations` (server) in the same component

## Testing

- Verify all locale JSON files have identical key structures (use a CI lint script)
- Test locale switching: navigate, switch locale, verify URL and content change
- Test fallback: request unsupported locale → should 404 or redirect to default
- Test SEO: verify `<link rel="alternate" hreflang="...">` tags in page source
- Test plural forms in all supported locales (rules differ between languages)
- Use `next-intl`'s TypeScript integration for compile-time key checking
